# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Leonid Kahle et al. (2024). A dual-cutoff machine-learned potential for condensed organic systems obtained via uncertainty-guided active learning.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2408.03058  arXiv:2408.03058v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2408.03058v1 (sha256 a95bd8c3007bc781...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 297 (Training/reliability). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/kahle2024.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the final dual-cutoff ACE potential (short-range cutoff
# 3 A for all pairs, long-range cutoff 7 A for C-C) trained with pacemaker
# on 2,641 revPBE-vdW configurations from 18 active-learning steps, with
# its test energy and force RMSEs. Densities, vibrational frequencies,
# heat capacities, vaporisation enthalpies and diffusion coefficients are
# properties, not error metrics.

